[size=4][b]Description[/b][/size]
The game's [b]corpses highlight[/b] key ([b]V[/b] by default) now also highlights [b]lootable containers[/b]: crates, boxes, vehicles and guns that have items inside. Highlighted containers get the outline and the [b]examine[/b] cursor, so you can open them straight from the V mode instead of hunting for them.

Client-side and purely visual: works in single player and multiplayer, causes no desync, and the other players don't need it.

[size=4][b]Installation instructions[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Download the zip from the Files tab.[/*]
[*]Extract it into the game folder, the one that contains [b]binaries[/b] and [b]mods[/b], e.g. [i]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Call to Arms - Gates of Hell[/i]. If Windows asks, overwrite [b]version.dll[/b]: it's the same file in all my mods. [b]If you use GOHSE[/b] (Gates of Hell Script Extender), don't overwrite it: keep GOHSE's version.dll, and the script the zip puts in [i]gohse/mods/goh_dll_mods[/i] loads the mod.[/*]
[*]Start the game and press [b]V[/b].[/*]
[/list]After installing you should have:
[code]<game>\binaries\x64\version.dll
<game>\binaries\x64\goh_mods\loot_highlight.dll
<game>\gohse\mods\goh_dll_mods\   (used only with GOHSE)[/code][b]Uninstall:[/b] delete [i]binaries\x64\goh_mods\loot_highlight.dll[/i]. If you have none of my other mods installed, also delete [i]binaries\x64\version.dll[/i], the [i]goh_mods[/i] folder and [i]gohse\mods\goh_dll_mods[/i].

[size=4][b]Main features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]V highlights crates, boxes and other static inventories that hold items.[/*]
[*]V highlights vehicles and guns with items in their inventory (except your own).[/*]
[*]Highlighted containers show the examine cursor and can be opened directly from the V mode.[/*]
[*]Empty containers and objects hidden in the fog of war are not highlighted, so it gives no unfair info.[/*]
[*]Fixes V randomly turning off while the key is still held down.[/*]
[*]The game files on disk are never modified: the DLL patches the game in memory only. If a game update changes the code it needs, it skips that part and the game runs unmodded.[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Call to Arms - Gates of Hell: Ostfront, x64, tested on game versions [b]1.067.0[/b] and [b]1.069.0[/b].[/*]
[*]Works with or without [url=https://github.com/nature2468/gohse]GOHSE[/url], the Gates of Hell Script Extender (from the 1.0.3 version).[/*]
[*]No other mods needed. The mod loader ([b]version.dll[/b]) is included in the zip.[/*]
[/list]Troubleshooting log: [i]%TEMP%\goh_loot_highlight_call_to_arms.exe.log[/i]

[size=4][b]Source code[/b][/size]
Open source, built from a single C file. Source, build instructions and my other Gates of Hell mods (Coop Game Speed, Coop Checkpoint, Inspect Preview): [url=https://github.com/nicko996/goh-coop-mods]github.com/nicko996/goh-coop-mods[/url]

